id: pm-6xlyss
title: "Absence-tolerant readers accept only ENOENT, so a tracker root that is a regular file raises an unclassified fault instead of the typed refusal the guard already owns — and that fault blocks the daily release"
description: ""
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:ci","area:sdk",defect-recurrence,error-taxonomy,gate,refusal-typing,release-blocker
created_at: "2026-08-10T05:50:32.166Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T16:47:20.991Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: readWorkspaceContextIntentContracts treats ENOTDIR as absence so the authoritative tracker-root guard emits the refusal; A shared isFileAbsentError helper expresses the ENOENT/ENOTDIR equivalence in one place; A ratchet gate fails any NEW catch clause that tolerates ENOENT without ENOTDIR; The remaining 45 declared sites are reviewed per-site and the ceiling reaches 0
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "pm-cli 2026.8.9, node v26.5.0, linux; observed in production telemetry and reproduced locally"
repro_steps: 1. touch ./notadir  2. pm list --path ./notadir
expected_result: "A typed usage/not-found refusal (PmCliError), which shouldCaptureCliError excludes from Sentry."
actual_result: "Raw Node ENOTDIR escapes as unclassified_runtime_error, is captured to Sentry as PM-CLI-2X 'Error: ENOTDIR: not a directory, open', classified unexpected_fault, and fails sentry-telemetry-gate (max_high 0) — blocking every daily Auto Release cut."
component: "sdk/context-intent-runtime, core/fs/fs-utils, release/sentry-telemetry-gate"
