comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T16:47:20.038Z","harness:codex","Scope disposition: the live zero-ceiling migration spans 45 catch clauses across 29 core/SDK modules and requires per-site filesystem semantic review. It is not coupled to the SDK refusal/recovery contract implementation selected for this PR, so no source edit is being made under this item and the claim is released immediately."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:51:29.524Z","harness:claude-code",probe
  "2026-08-10T05:52:24.862Z","harness:claude-code",The gate that blocked the release was right; the event it blocked on was the bug. Asking 'could this fault have been a refusal?' is the cheaper question than asking 'is this gate too strict?'.
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:52:24.862Z","harness:claude-code","An authoritative guard is only as good as its position in the pipeline. tracker_root_not_directory was correct, tested, and unreachable, because a later-added optional read ran before it. Ordering, not absence, was the defect."
  "2026-08-10T05:52:24.862Z","harness:claude-code","For an optional read, ENOENT and ENOTDIR are the same answer reached from different directions. Any absence-tolerant reader that accepts only ENOENT converts a graceful default into an unclassified fault the moment a path component is a regular file - and an untyped fault is the one thing the release gate cannot forgive."
