  npx vitest run tests/unit/core/fs/fs-utils.spec.ts,tests/unit/core/fs/fs-utils.spec.ts,project
body: "## What the record shows\n\nThe daily scheduled Auto Release run failed on `sentry-telemetry-gate` with `max_high: 0` and one blocking issue:\n\n```\n\"blocking_short_ids\": [\"PM-CLI-2X\"],\n\"blocking_titles\": [\"Error: ENOTDIR: not a directory, open\"],\n\"blocking_reasons\": [{\"short_id\": \"PM-CLI-2X\", \"reason\": \"unexpected_fault\"}]\n```\n\nThe gate is correct. The event is a genuine unclassified fault. The defect is that it should never have been a fault at all.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`readWorkspaceContextIntentContracts` reads the optional `context-intents.json` and tolerates only `ENOENT`:\n\n```ts\nif (isRecord(error) && typeof error.code === \"string\" && error.code === \"ENOENT\") return [];\nthrow error;\n```\n\nWhen the tracker root is a regular file, Node reports `ENOTDIR`, not `ENOENT`. For an **optional** read those two errno values answer the same question - the file is not there and cannot be there - but only one of them is accepted, so the raw error escapes.\n\nThe guard that owns this refusal already exists and is correct. `assertItemMetadataRoot` in `core/store/item-store.ts` raises a typed `tracker_root_not_directory` usage refusal for exactly this state. It simply never runs: the optional declaration read happens **earlier in the command pipeline** and throws first.\n\nThis is the recurrence family owned by pm-7rrqsk - a newer read path added without picking up an established guard. The consequence chain is what makes it expensive:\n\nuntyped fault -> `shouldCaptureCliError` returns true -> Sentry `unexpected_fault` -> release gate `max_high` breached -> every daily cut blocked.\n\n## Population\n\nAn AST scan of `src/**/*.ts` for catch clauses that name `ENOENT` without `ENOTDIR` found **45** sites after the two central fixes. Most are not reachable from a misdirected root today, but each is the same latent shape, and any one of them can become the next release blocker the same way this one did.\n\n## Disposition\n\nShipped in this change:\n\n- `isFileAbsentError` in `core/fs/fs-utils.ts` states the equivalence once; `readFileIfExists` and `removeFileIfExists` adopt it.\n- `sdk/context-intent-runtime.ts` uses it, so the authoritative root guard now speaks instead of the optional reader.\n- `scripts/release/absence-tolerance-gate.mjs` ratchets the population. The bound fails in **both** directions: a higher count is a regression, a lower one is an undeclared improvement that must be written down so the next regression cannot hide beneath slack.\n\nLeft open by this item: driving the declared ceiling from 45 to 0 by reviewing each remaining site, since a blind rewrite would wrongly silence readers where `ENOTDIR` really does mean corruption rather than absence.\n\n## Verification\n\n`pm list --path <a regular file>` now exits 3 with a typed refusal and is not captured to Sentry."
